# Untracked, machine-local, and copied into the production image by
# `COPY ylaneenkasvit` in Dockerfile unless it is excluded here: a developer's
# copy switches DEBUG on and opens ALLOWED_HOSTS, and since upgrade plan Stage
# 0 it also appends `django_extensions` -- which the production image does not
# install, so an image built in a working checkout died on `ImportError: No
# module named django_extensions` instead of silently running in debug. The
# development image is unaffected either way: it has no app code at all and
# reads the working copy from the /src bind mount, which is where its
# local_settings.py is supposed to come from.
